1
00:04:25,714 --> 00:04:31,714
A Movie Like No Other

2
00:08:51,428 --> 00:08:57,428
Moonwalker is a fantasy, music film directed by Colin Chilvers.

3
00:13:17,142 --> 00:13:23,142
This fantastical movie inspired by the music of Michael Jackson features
imaginative interpretations of hit tracks from the iconic 1987 album “Bad”.

4
00:17:42,857 --> 00:17:48,857
Michael, played by Michael Jackson.

5
00:22:08,571 --> 00:22:14,571
Mr. Big, played by Joe Pesci.

6
00:26:34,285 --> 00:26:40,285
Sean, played by Sean Ono Lennon.

7
00:31:00,000 --> 00:31:06,000
Katie, played by Kelley Parker.

8
00:35:25,714 --> 00:35:31,714
Zeke, played by Brandon Quintin Adams.

9
00:39:51,428 --> 00:39:57,428
Maestro (segment "Badder"), played by Ben Aaron.

10
00:44:17,142 --> 00:44:23,142
Moonwalker is a 1988 American experimental anthology
musical film starring Michael Jackson.

11
00:48:42,857 --> 00:48:48,857
Rather than featuring one continuous narrative, the film expresses the influence of fandom and innocence through a
collection of short films about Jackson, several of which are long-form music videos from Jackson's 1987 album Bad.

12
00:53:08,571 --> 00:53:14,571
The film is named after the dance technique known as the
moonwalk, which Jackson was known for performing.

13
00:57:34,285 --> 00:57:40,285
The film was released theatrically in Europe and South America, but Warner Bros.

14
01:02:00,000 --> 01:02:06,000
canceled plans for a Christmas 1988 theatrical release in the United States.

15
01:06:25,714 --> 01:06:31,714
Moonwalker was released on VHS, and remained #1 on
Billboard's Video Chart for 22 weeks.

16
01:10:51,428 --> 01:10:57,428
Moonwalker also spent 14 weeks at #1 on Billboards Top Video- Cassette sales chart In 1989, Moonwalker was honoured
with a certification of 800,000 copies sold by the Recording Industry Association of America (RIAA).

17
01:15:17,142 --> 01:15:23,142
Moonwalker has been certified 9 x Platinum in the United Kingdom.

18
01:19:42,857 --> 01:19:48,857
The "Leave Me Alone" video aired as a separate entity and won a Grammy in 1990 for Best Music
Video, Short Form, which is the only Grammy Award Jackson received for the album Bad.

19
01:24:08,571 --> 01:24:14,571
"Leave Me Alone" video also won the Cannes Gold
Lion Award for Best Special Effects.

20
01:28:34,285 --> 01:28:40,285
The film explores themes of dancing, drug crime, gangster, entertainer, parody.
